            <ArticleTitle>Three unusual presentations of interscapular back pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1000-1, 1004</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Three cases of central thoracic back pain are presented. All were diagnostic brain teasers that baffled several practitioners and consultants. The cases represented unusual presentations of malignant disease, myocardial infarction and duodenal ulceration.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
